--- implementation boundary ---
E1 source is ordinary C with one hidden __thread integer initialized to 42, tls_model(initial-exec), and one exported GetTLS function that returns the variable.
E1 was built with fixed OHOS x86_64 clang, -fno-emulated-tls, and -ftls-model=initial-exec so the final object contains real ELF TLS rather than compiler-emulated TLS.
E1 contains no Go source or runtime, no res_search reference, no NODELETE flag, and no SYMBOLIC flag.
E4 source directly references Hello and RuntimeProbe in an exported function, but runNeededProbe only calls dlopen on libneededprobe.so and never resolves or calls that function.
E4 links against the existing ignored libgoprobe.so so libneededprobe.so records DT_NEEDED libgoprobe.so and RUNPATH $ORIGIN.
C++ runTlsProbe and runNeededProbe call dlopen with RTLD_NOW|RTLD_LOCAL, capture errno before dlerror, preserve the original dlerror string, retain successful handles, and return structured loader observations through Node-API.
The TestRunner first verifies ping=pong and the fixed version, then runs E1 and E4 in that order; an exact expected loader rejection satisfies the experiment observation assertion but remains functional=BLOCKED.
No runGoProbe call, Go build, c-archive build, netgo build, Go export call, DNS lookup, socket probe, or NetBird operation was executed.

--- native probe build and correction ---
The first build attempt was preceded by shellcheck, which is unavailable on this host; the chained command stopped before any build and no shellcheck result is claimed.
A subsequent initial native build showed OHOS clang had emitted __emutls_get_address and no real TLS relocation despite the variable attribute; that invalid intermediate was not packaged or run.
The build script was corrected before cold HAP build to add -fno-emulated-tls and -ftls-model=initial-exec.
