--- interpretation and boundary ---
E1 removes Go, res_search, NODELETE, SYMBOLIC, and dependency-chain variables while retaining a real initial-exec TLS relocation; the same measured loader rejects this ordinary late-loaded shared object before GetTLS.
E4 removes direct libgoprobe dlopen as the entry operation and instead uses a correctly linked $ORIGIN DT_NEEDED wrapper; the runtime dlopen chain still reaches libgoprobe.so late and fails before either direct reference is called.
Together E1 and E4 close the direct and transitive no-fork late-load variants for this exact API 24 x86_64 TestRunner process and these verified ELF inputs.
E4 is not process-startup linkage, does not establish startup static-TLS behavior, and does not test an executable with libgoprobe.so loaded before process initialization.
The result does not generalize to arm64, named physical devices, a separate process, a patched Go runtime/toolchain, another system image, another loader, or product support.
No NetBird, WireGuard, VPN, TUN, DNS, public network, UIAbility, physical-device, signing, channel, or product-support path was exercised.
verdict=blocked
r1_exit=no
