The experiments are project-local probes and do not modify NetBird, WireGuard, Go runtime, or another fixed upstream, so the upstream adaptation patch count remains 0 and no existing patch-budget threshold was exceeded.
The measured no-fork in-process late-load route is now blocked; selecting a separate-process boundary or a patched Go runtime/toolchain would materially change the cross-language architecture or introduce a potential high-maintenance fork, so roadmap and evidence-schema T0 rules require route discussion before either implementation begins.
